WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.821
Workflow gives AI work a process. Here's how ours works.
Workflow 为 AI 工作提供流程。下面看看我们的实现。

2
00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:08.599
AI workflows define stages, dependencies, and branches.
AI 工作流定义阶段、依赖关系与分支。

3
00:00:08.949 --> 00:00:11.354
Plan decides whether we need outside data.
Plan 决定是否需要外部数据。

4
00:00:11.704 --> 00:00:14.849
If so, Lookup fetches it with a deterministic tool.
如果需要，Lookup 使用确定性工具获取数据。

5
00:00:15.199 --> 00:00:18.396
Otherwise, Draft starts immediately, using model judgment.
否则，Draft 立即开始，通过模型判断来写作。

6
00:00:18.746 --> 00:00:21.236
If the task needs lookup, drafting waits.
任务需要查询时，写作阶段就要等待。

7
00:00:22.936 --> 00:00:29.523
Our Host owns authoritative Run state, dependencies, routing, execution records, and mechanical checks.
Host 掌握 Run 的权威状态，负责依赖、路由、执行记录与机械检查。

8
00:00:29.873 --> 00:00:35.051
Main, the initiating conversation, makes semantic decisions and assigns stages through Host.
Main 就是发起任务的会话，负责语义决策，并通过 Host 分配阶段。

9
00:00:35.401 --> 00:00:39.665
Host creates a Main worker: an isolated, temporary stage context.
Host 创建 Main worker：一个隔离的临时阶段上下文。

10
00:00:40.015 --> 00:00:44.380
The worker returns results. Host records execution and checks delivery.
Worker 返回结果；Host 记录执行并检查交付。

11
00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:49.044
Main accepts delivery, combining its judgment with Host's execution authority.
Main 结合自身判断与 Host 的执行权威，验收交付结果。

12
00:00:50.744 --> 00:00:55.385
A Harness connects models, tools, the environment, and the execution lifecycle.
Harness 连接模型、工具、环境与执行生命周期。

13
00:00:55.735 --> 00:00:59.007
A Workflow supplies the task process that the harness runs.
Workflow 提供由 Harness 执行的任务流程。

14
00:00:59.357 --> 00:01:02.520
A Skill supplies reusable instructions and tool assets.
Skill 提供可复用的指令与工具资源。

15
00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:07.201
Converting a Skill to a Workflow must preserve its tools and operating boundaries.
将 Skill 转成 Workflow，必须保留其工具与操作边界。

16
00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:11.994
Host routes Stage A into an isolated context.
Host 将阶段 A 路由到隔离上下文。

17
00:01:12.344 --> 00:01:14.634
Stage B gets its own relevant history.
阶段 B 得到与自己有关的历史信息。

18
00:01:14.984 --> 00:01:17.180
A Reviewer role can serve Stage A.
Reviewer 角色可以服务于阶段 A。

19
00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:21.752
The same role can serve Stage B. Roles and node identities differ.
同一个角色也可以服务于阶段 B。角色与节点身份不同。

20
00:01:23.452 --> 00:01:27.209
Stage A and Stage B share input, without depending on each other.
阶段 A 与阶段 B 共享输入，但彼此没有依赖。

21
00:01:27.559 --> 00:01:33.164
Reusable common context, or caching where supported, can reduce repeated setup for Stage B.
复用公共上下文，或在支持时使用缓存，可以减少阶段 B 的重复准备。

22
00:01:33.514 --> 00:01:35.672
Independent stages can run in parallel.
独立阶段可以并行执行。

23
00:01:36.022 --> 00:01:39.200
Join waits for both results before dependent work starts.
Join 等待两份结果到齐后，再启动依赖它们的工作。

24
00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:44.784
Bounded context, caching, and parallel work may bring Gains.
限定上下文、缓存与并行，可能带来收益。

25
00:01:45.134 --> 00:01:49.691
Overhead from handoffs and cold starts can outweigh those gains on small jobs.
小任务中，交接与冷启动开销可能超过这些收益。

26
00:01:50.041 --> 00:01:55.464
Measure each Result. This architecture guarantees neither lower cost nor lower latency.
衡量每次结果。这种架构既不保证成本更低，也不保证延迟更短。
